    "text": "If ⟨Ω, ⩽⟩ is the countable universal poset, then G = Aut (⟨Ω, ⩽⟩) is simple\n(A. M. W. Glass, S. H. McCleary, M. Rubin, Math. Z., 214, no. 1 (1993), 55–66). If H\nis a subgroup of G such that |G : H| < 2ℵ0 and H is transitive on Ω, does H = G?\n                                                                                   A. M. W. Glass",
